From 8c134c3a7a50bfa12b9c917e5075c31e34948692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 12:43:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ADR-0007: presence confirmation latches per delta baseline

Fixes a real actuator-flapping incident distinct from ADR-0006's: during
the same logged shower, the mmWave presence sensor toggled False/True
every 20-100+ seconds throughout continuous, attended use (a common
mmWave failure mode -- a person standing relatively still washing looks
like "no motion"). Several gaps exceeded the 60s
presence_confirmation_window_seconds. Replaying the real humidity/presence
values through the unchanged DecisionEngine shows the consequence
directly: WATER_CUT <-> WATER_AVAILABLE toggled roughly six times in 13
minutes while the person was still in the shower and the humidity delta
stayed far above threshold the whole time -- each toggle would have fired
the actuator script again, cycling a physical valve/pump mid-shower.

Root cause: evaluate() re-derives "is presence confirmed" fresh on every
call from `now - last_presence_at` alone, treating a momentary sensor
gap as equivalent to "this humidity rise is no longer confirmed as
shower-caused" -- even though ADR-0003's own stated purpose for the
presence check is causation confirmation, not real-time occupancy
tracking.

Fix: DecisionEngine now latches presence confirmation per delta baseline.
Once confirmed for the current active_since_humidity baseline, a later
gap can't alone flip an already-cut decision back to available while
delta remains exceeded. The latch resets on IDLE/no-session or whenever
active_since_humidity itself changes (fresh STARTED, or a sibling's
RESUMED) -- the same reset points the delta baseline already uses. It
never overrides a genuine delta decline; it only matters while delta is
still over threshold.

Replaying the full incident with this fix and ADR-0006's fix together
drops the day's total decision changes from ~9 (7 flapping toggles
during the shower + never resolving) down to 3: idle -> cut (at the
real start) -> available (at the real, correctly-detected end) -> stays
available for the rest of the day.

No new config keys. presence_confirmation_window_seconds keeps its
existing meaning (how recent a sighting must be for the FIRST
confirmation) -- this ADR removes the ongoing re-litigation of a
confirmation that's already been established. replay.py needs no
changes since it already constructs one DecisionEngine per run.

- decision.py: DecisionEngine gains _latched_baseline /
  _presence_confirmed_latch instance state. evaluate() resets both on
  IDLE/no-session and on active_since_humidity change; sets the latch
  True on first confirmation; checks the latch before deciding to cut.
  This is a deliberate, documented departure from evaluate() being a
  fully stateless pure function (docstring updated accordingly).
- const.py / __init__.py / manifest.json: version bump only (1.8.0).
- Tests: 7 new tests in test_decision.py covering the latch persisting
  through a later out-of-window gap, no latch before first
  confirmation, latch reset on fresh baseline (sibling RESUMED), latch
  reset on return to IDLE, genuine decline still overriding the latch
  (with the latch still holding if delta rises again same baseline),
  and a regression test replaying the exact logged gap pattern. Full
  suite: 116 passed (110 previously passing + 6 in test_decision.py
  ... see file for exact count).
- README.md / BACKLOG.md updated.

See adr/ADR-0007-presence-confirmation-latch.md for full rationale,
including alternatives considered (a longer window alone; a separate
slow-release window; moving this into Session Detection instead).
